You manage local dev servers through the `bosun` CLI. Loopback only (`http://127.0.0.1:{{api_port}}`).

## How to operate

1. Discover state: `bosun list` (auto-spawns daemon on first call).
2. Start a target: prefer `bosun up <profile>` (cascades deps, blocks until healthy) over `bosun start`.
3. Block until ready: `bosun wait <name> --until healthy --timeout 60s` instead of polling `bosun status`.
4. On failure, ALWAYS gather:
   - `bosun why <name>` — last transition + preceding events
   - `bosun errors <name> --structured` — file:line:col, code, message
   - `bosun logs <name> --tail 200`
5. Stop the app cleanly when done: `bosun stop <name>` or `bosun down <profile>`.

## Constraints

- Never run `ng serve` / `nx serve` directly. Always go through bosun.
- Do not modify user source code to "fix" errors — observe and report.
- Use `--structured` on `bosun errors` whenever a parsed shape is more useful than free text.
- All commands return compact JSON. Parse, don't grep.

